Addition from Ivan: besides logs and score, follow what the run page UI shows, i.e. what the agent types, selects and clicks in each browser, and its screens over time. The UI at https://ehl-challenge.atira.ai/runs/run_57f15cb68ad9f88a shows this; `atira.cmd help mcp` says the CLI's MCP server exposes "a browser's screen at a time, recorded inputs". Find the API endpoints behind that:
- try `atira.cmd help mcp`;
- look at https://ehl-challenge.atira.ai/llms-full.txt for endpoints such as /v1/runs/{id}/inputs, /screens, /events or /browsers;
- or speak MCP over stdio to `atira.cmd mcp` with a small Python script that sends initialize, tools/list, then tools/call.

Use the same x-api-key header. If an endpoint gives screenshots, you may view a few at key moments (e.g. the ERP search, the configurator), but describe them only as actions and page kinds ("typed into the ERP search field, selected a filter, opened a detail page"). Never print typed text, field values, numbers, codes or addresses. Mask them as before.

Use this to answer, per browser:
- the sequence of actions in phases;
- where it got stuck or repeated itself (same click or page several times, empty searches, dialogs, logins, paging);
- how long each phase took;
- especially on the ERP: what it searched by, whether it opened candidate details, and whether it filtered by group.

Add to your report a section "What the browsers did", under 250 extra words.

